 as std::cin; do not use using declarations or directives.\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"REQ026\", \"category\": \"source_code\", \"description\": \"Require std::endl for output line endings as the chosen project convention.\", \"expression\": null, \"literal_strings\": [\"std::endl\"], \"visibility\": \"student_visible\", \"sources\": [{\"page\": 1, \"section\": \"Public tests /7\", \"evidence\": \"Require std::endl for output line endings as the chosen project convention.\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"REQ027\", \"category\": \"source_code\", \"description\": \"Use scalar variables; do not use arrays or containers for the calculation.\", \"expression\": null, \"literal_strings\": [], \"visibility\": \"student_visible\", \"sources\": [{\"page\": 1, \"section\": \"Public tests /7\", \"evidence\": \"Use scalar variables; do not use arrays or containers for the calculation.\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"REQ028\", \"category\": \"numerical_comparison\", \"description\": \"Tests compare with the reference estimate r (the first new estimate satisfying the stated stopping rule), not only with sqrt(n); the starting guess and tolerance affect the expected answer.\", \"expression\": null, \"literal_strings\": [], \"visibility\": \"student_visible\", \"sources\": [{\"page\": 2, \"section\": \"Release tests /13\", \"evidence\": \"The reference implementation starts at the supplied s and returns the first new estimate satisfying the stated stopping rule. Tests compare with that estimate r, not only with sqrt(n)\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"REQ029\", \"category\": \"numerical_comparison\", \"description\": \"Require a finite, non-negative result z within the grader's comparison allowance of the reference estimate r; this allowance is separate from the user-supplied e.\", \"expression\": \"|z - r| <= 1e-12 * max(1, |r|)\", \"literal_strings\": [], \"visibility\": \"student_visible\", \"sources\": [{\"page\": 2, \"section\": \"Release tests /13\", \"evidence\": \"Require a finite, non-negative result z with |z -