: [-8, 6], \"transformation\": \"n = 10^u\"}, {\"variable\": \"v\", \"distribution\": \"uniform\", \"bounds\": [-3, 4], \"transformation\": \"s = 10^v\"}, {\"variable\": \"w\", \"distribution\": \"uniform\", \"bounds\": [-10, -1], \"transformation\": \"e = 10^w\"}], \"seed\": null, \"invalid_input_policy\": \"Prepend invalid values in every fifth run.\", \"acceptance_filters\": \"Verify termination and finite intermediates before adding a generated case; avoid generated cases whose stopping decision depends on rounding at the tolerance boundary (S100 already tests equality using exactly representable values).\", \"oracle_requirement_ids\": [\"REQ001\", \"REQ003\", \"REQ004\", \"REQ029\"], \"sources\": [{\"page\": 4, \"section\": \"Secret tests /8\", \"evidence\": \"S107_private_batch ... Reference and reproducibility: ... Verify termination and finite intermediates before adding a generated case. Avoid generated cases whose stopping decision depends on rounding at the tolerance boundary.\"}]}, \"sources\": [{\"page\": 4, \"section\": \"Secret tests /8\", \"evidence\": \"S107_private_batch\"}]}\n  ],\n  \"out_of_scope\": [\n    {\"id\": \"OOS001\", \"description\": \"Malformed input, early end-of-file, NaN, infinity, overflow, and tolerance values that prevent convergence because of rounding are outside this draft's scope.\", \"sources\": [{\"page\": 3, \"section\": \"Notes and known issues\", \"evidence\": \"Malformed input, early end-of-file, NaN, infinity, overflow, and tolerance values that prevent convergence because of rounding are outside this draft's scope.\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"OOS002\", \"description\": \"Execution speed is not scored.\", \"sources\": [{\"page\": 3, \"section\": \"Notes and known issues\", \"evidence\": \"A generous timeout detects non-termination; speed is not scored.\"}]}\n  ],\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\"id\": \"ISS001\", \"type\": \"ambiguity\", \"description\": \"The blocking-test configuration is described as 'proposed', not confirmed; the grading consequence of a skipped or blocked test is not specified.\", \"affected_ids\": [\"EXE001\", \"G002\"], \"sources\": [{\"page\": 1, \"section\": \"Public tests /7\", \"evidence\": \"In the proposed configuration, all tests are blocking tests: release tests run only after all pass.\"}], \"requires_review\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"ISS002\", \"type\": \"missing_information\", \"description\": \"No single overall total is explicitly stated. Per-group totals (7, 13, 8) are explicit and the document explicitly states 7 + 13 = 20 for public + release, but the overall total (derived 28) is not given as a stated value.\", \"affected_ids\": [\"G001\", \"G002\", \"G003\"], \"sources\": [{\"page\": 2, \"section\": \"Release tests /13\", \"evidence\": \"The public and release tests contribute 7 + 13 = 20 marks.\"}, {\"page\": 4, \"section\": \"Secret tests /8\", \"evidence\": \"Secret tests /8\"}], \"requires_review\": false},\n    {\"id\": \"ISS003\", \"type\": \"missing_information\", \"description\": \"The S107 private fixed seed value is not provided in the document (only described as a 'private fixed seed'), so the generated batch cannot be reproduced from the document alone; it is recorded in the instructor's test fixture.\", \"affected_ids\": [\"S107\"], \"sources\": [{\"page\": 4, \"section\": \"Secret tests /8\", \"evidence\": \"Using a private fixed seed, generate 40 triples ... Record the generated triples, seed, and oracle outputs in the instructor's test fixture.\"}], \"requires_review\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"ISS004\", \"type\": \"ambiguity\", \"description\": \"R112 specifies 'repeated invalid inputs across all three prompts' and 'valid cases such as ...' without giving the exact ordered token sequence, so the run's full input is not fully determined by the document.\", \"affected_ids\": [\"R112\"], \"sources\": [{\"page\": 2, \"section\": \"Release tests /13\", \"evidence\": \"R112_mixed_trials: Combine repeated invalid inputs across all three prompts with valid cases such as (10^-8, 1, 10^-10) and (10^6, 10, 10^-6).\"}], \"requires_review\": true}\n  ],\n  \"feedback_issue_types\": [\n    {\"id\": \"FIT001\", \"type\": \"input_validation\", \"description\": \"Accepted and rejected values for n, s, e may not follow the stated input contract (n>=0, s>0, e>0), or the wrong prompt may be repeated on invalid input.\", \"requirement_ids\": [\"REQ011\", \"REQ012\", \"REQ013\"], \"test_ids\": [\"R109\", \"R110\", \"R111\", \"R112\", \"S106\"], \"classification_origin\": \"suggested_mapping\", \"evidence_needed\": \"Observed prompt sequence and which values were accepted/rejected for each run, compared to the contract.\", \"alternative_explanations\": [\"Off-by-one in the validity comparison operator\", \"Reading the wrong variable for a prompt\"], \"feedback_template\": \"Check how your program handles values outside the permitted range for each input. Does it reject the right values and re-ask only the matching prompt?\", \"sources\": [{\"page\": 3, \"section\": \"Notes and known issues\", \"evidence\": \"Reject n < 0, s <= 0, and e <= 0. Repeat only the corresponding prompt, with no additional error message.\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"FIT002\", \"type\": \"state_preservation\", \"description\": \"Previously accepted values (n, s) may be lost or changed when a later prompt is repeated.\", \"requirement_ids\": [\"REQ014\"], \"test_ids\": [\"R110\", \"R111\", \"S106\"], \"classification_origin\": \"suggested_mapping\", \"evidence_needed\": \"Whether the final computation used the originally accepted n and s after re-prompting a later field.\", \"alternative_explanations\": [\"Variables overwritten during re-prompting\", \"Re-reading all inputs from scratch\"], \"feedback_template\": \"When you re-ask one prompt, are the values you already accepted still intact? Trace which variables hold n and s after the loop.\", \"sources\": [{\"page\": 3, \"section\": \"Notes and known issues\", \"evidence\": \"Keep previously accepted values.\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"FIT003\", \"type\": \"algorithm_compliance\", \"description\": \"The implementation may not follow the required Newton update, or may use a root/power routine or a non-change-based stopping rule.\", \"requirement_ids\": [\"REQ001\", \"REQ009\", \"REQ006\"], \"test_ids\": [\"P101\", \"S102\", \"S103\", \"S104\"], \"classification_origin\": \"suggested_mapping\", \"evidence_needed\": \"Source inspection for the update expression and absence of sqrt/pow; runtime results on residual-trap and guess-sensitivity cases.\", \"alternative_explanations\": [\"Using a squared-residual or relative stopping rule\", \"Substituting a fixed starting guess\"], \"feedback_template\": \"Confirm your loop applies the stated update to the current estimate and stops based on the change between successive estimates, not on the residual or a fixed count.\", \"sources\": [{\"page\": 3, \"section\": \"Notes and known issues\", \"evidence\": \"Implement the Newton update using arithmetic and a loop. Do not use sqrt, pow, or equivalent root-solving routines.\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"FIT004\", \"type\": \"termination\", \"description\": \"The loop may stop at the wrong point or return the wrong estimate (old vs new).\", \"requirement_ids\": [\"REQ003\", \"REQ004\"], \"test_ids\": [\"S100\", \"S101\", \"R101\"], \"classification_origin\": \"suggested_mapping\", \"evidence_needed\": \"The estimate returned and the iteration at which the loop stopped for boundary and exact-guess cases.\", \"alternative_explanations\": [\"Returning x_k instead of x_{k+1}\", \"Checking the condition before the first update\"], \"feedback_template\": \"Trace the state immediately before and after an iteration. Which estimate do you print, and at which point does your program decide to stop?\", \"sources\": [{\"page\": 1, \"section\": \"Learning objectives\", \"evidence\": \"Stop at the first update satisfying |x_{k+1} - x_k| <= e and output x_{k+1}.\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"FIT005\", \"type\": \"boundary_condition\", \"description\": \"The equality case in the stopping condition (change exactly equal to e) may be mishandled.\", \"requirement_ids\": [\"REQ003\"], \"test_ids\": [\"S100\", \"R101\"], \"classification_origin\": \"suggested_mapping\", \"evidence_needed\": \"Behaviour when the change between successive estimates is exactly equal to the tolerance.\", \"alternative_explanations\": [\"Using < instead of <= in the stopping test\"], \"feedback_template\": \"Review the boundary case where the change equals the tolerance. Does your stopping condition handle equality consistently?\", \"sources\": [{\"page\": 3, \"section\": \"Notes and known issues\", \"evidence\": \"Include equality in the stopping condition: (n, s, e) = (2, 1, 0.5) must stop after one update.\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"FIT006\", \"type\": \"special_case\", \"description\": \"The n = 0 case may be mishandled (division by zero, or skipping validation of s and e).\", \"requirement_ids\": [\"REQ005\", \"REQ015\"], \"test_ids\": [\"R100\", \"S106\"], \"classification_origin\": \"suggested_mapping\", \"evidence_needed\": \"Whether all three inputs are read and validated for n=0 and whether zero is returned without a division by zero.\", \"alternative_explanations\": [\"Short-circuiting to zero before reading s and e\", \"Entering the iteration loop for n=0\"], \"feedback_template\": \"For a zero radicand, does your program still read and validate all three inputs before printing zero, and avoid dividing by zero?\", \"sources\": [{\"page\": 1, \"section\": \"Learning objectives\", \"evidence\": \"For n = 0, read and validate all three inputs, then output zero directly.\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"FIT007\", \"type\": \"numerical_precision\", \"description\": \"Integer arithmetic, truncation, or insufficient precision may affect the result.\", \"requirement_ids\": [\"REQ007\"], \"test_ids\": [\"R106\", \"R104\"], \"classification_origin\": \"suggested_mapping\", \"evidence_needed\": \"Result values on non-square and fractional inputs compared to the double-precision oracle.\", \"alternative_explanations\": [\"Using int variables for n, s, or the estimate\", \"Integer division in the update\"], \"feedback_template\": \"Inspect the types and intermediate calculations. Could integer arithmetic or truncation be losing information before the result is printed?\", \"sources\": [{\"page\": 3, \"section\": \"Notes and known issues\", \"evidence\": \"Use double for n, s, e, and the estimates.\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"FIT008\", \"type\": \"output_format\", \"description\": \"The result line may violate the label, precision, line-ending, or no-extra-output contract.\", \"requirement_ids\": [\"REQ016\", \"REQ018\", \"REQ019\", \"REQ020\", \"REQ021\", \"REQ026\"], \"test_ids\": [\"P103\", \"P106\"], \"classification_origin\": \"suggested_mapping\", \"evidence_needed\": \"The exact bytes of the prompt and result lines, including label, precision, and line endings.\", \"alternative_explanations\": [\"Missing 'Square root:' label\", \"Wrong setprecision\", \"Extra blank lines or iteration logs\", \"Using '\\\\n' instead of std::endl\"], \"feedback_template\": \"Compare your output with the published format, including the result label, the 17-significant-digit precision, line endings, and any extra lines.\", \"sources\": [{\"page\": 3, \"section\": \"Notes and known issues\", \"evidence\": \"Print one result line using the label Square root: and std::setprecision(17). ... Do not add iteration logs, extra numbers, or blank lines.\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"FIT009\", \"type\": \"source_restriction\", \"description\": \"The source may violate explicit restrictions (using-declarations, arrays/containers, disallowed headers, missing return 0).\", \"requirement_ids\": [\"REQ022\", \"REQ023\", \"REQ025\", \"REQ026\", \"REQ027\"], \"test_ids\": [\"P100\", \"P101\", \"P102\", \"P103\", \"P104\"], \"classification_origin\": \"suggested_mapping\", \"evidence_needed\": \"Source inspection for headers, using declarations/directives, qualified names, std::endl, scalar-only variables, and return 0;.\", \"alternative_explanations\": [\"Using 'using namespace std'\", \"Storing estimates in an array\", \"Including a disallowed header\"], \"feedback_template\": \"Check your source against the stated conventions: qualified standard-library names, the allowed headers, scalar variables, std::endl, and an explicit return 0;.\", \"sources\": [{\"page\": 1, \"section\": \"Public tests /7\", \"evidence\": \"P100_explicit_return ... P104_using_arrays\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"FIT010\", \"type\": \"result_correctness\", \"description\": \"Observed results may disagree with the required behaviour without an established cause.\", \"requirement_ids\": [\"REQ001\", \"REQ002\", \"REQ003\", \"REQ004\", \"REQ028\"], \"test_ids\": [\"R102\", \"R103\", \"R105\", \"R107\", \"R108\"], \"classification_origin\": \"suggested_mapping\", \"evidence_needed\": \"The returned value versus the reference first-new-estimate for the given (n, s, e).\", \"alternative_explanations\": [\"Wrong starting guess used\", \"Wrong stopping rule\", \"Precision loss\"], \"feedback_template\": \"The observed result does not match the required behaviour. Trace the intermediate estimates to locate the first divergence from the reference iteration.\", \"sources\": [{\"page\": 2, \"section\": \"Release tests /13\", \"evidence\": \"Tests compare with that estimate r, not only with sqrt(n), so the starting guess and tolerance affect the expected answer.\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"FIT011\", \"type\": \"input_parsing\", \"description\": \"Inputs may be read in the wrong order or representation.\", \"requirement_ids\": [\"REQ011\", \"REQ017\"], \"test_ids\": [\"P105\"], \"classification_origin\": \"suggested_mapping\", \"evidence_needed\": \"The order in which n, s, e are read and whether one value is consumed per prompt.\", \"alternative_explanations\": [\"Reading s before n\", \"Reading multiple values per prompt\"], \"feedback_template\": \"Confirm you read n, then s, then e, one value after each prompt, in that order.\", \"sources\": [{\"page\": 1, \"section\": \"Learning objectives\", \"evidence\": \"Read n >= 0, s > 0, and e > 0 in that order\"}]}\n  ],\n  \"review_required\": true\n}"
